EOS-CLA v1.0 — Eternal Open Substrate & Contributor Mutual Trust Agreement

This Eternal Open Substrate & Contributor License Agreement ("Agreement")
establishes a mutual trust framework between the Contributor (Human or
Autonomous Agent) and the Project Maintainers (8b.es and Péter József Lódri).
The goal of this Agreement is to guarantee that all submitted code, shaders,
algorithms, and assets remain free and open source for all eternity, while
providing absolute legal and operational liability protection for all
participating parties.

1. Definitions

- "Maintainers" (or "Us" / "We"): 8b.es, Péter József Lódri, and designated
  project custodians.
- "You" (or "Contributor"): The natural person, legal entity, or autonomous
  agent execution swarm (AIB) submitting code, shaders, documentation, or
  assets.
- "Contribution": Any code, WebAssembly module, GLSL/WGSL shader, spatial
  graph dataset, or documentation intentionally submitted for inclusion in
  the Project.
- "AIB / Autonomous Agent Contribution": Any code, synthetic asset, or
  optimization generated or piped directly by artificial intelligence
  systems, multi-agent swarms, or Model Context Protocol (MCP) gateways
  operating on behalf of the Contributor.

2. Eternal Open Source Grant & Ownership

- 2.1 Copyright License Grant: You retain full ownership of your
  Contribution. You hereby grant to the Maintainers and recipients of the
  Work a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, zero-cost, royalty-free,
  irrevocable copyright license to reproduce, prepare derivative works of,
  publicly display, sublicense, and distribute your Contribution.
- 2.2 Outbound Open Commitment: We promise to maintain the Work and all
  integrated Contributions under free and open-source licenses for all
  eternity.
- 2.3 Patent License Grant: You grant to the Maintainers and all users a
  perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable patent license to make, use, sell, or
  import the Work incorporating your Contribution.

3. AI Agent & Swarm Symbiosis (AIB Integration)

- 3.1 Synthetic Provenance: You explicitly affirm that any Contribution
  generated with or by Autonomous Agent Swarms (AIB), Large Language Models,
  or synthetic compiler pipelines is legally cleared for open-source
  distribution.
- 3.2 Capability-Graph Binding (G = (V, E, C)): Contributions submitted to
  the 8b.es network may be automatically mapped to capability-graph
  permission tokens C and assigned WebAssembly runtime boundaries without
  altering the underlying open-source license grant.

4. Absolute Disclaimer of Liability ("The Crash-and-Burn Clause")

- 4.1 AS-IS BASIS: ALL CONTRIBUTIONS AND SOFTWARE ARE PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS"
  AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND,
  EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF
  MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT.
- 4.2 TOTAL LIABILITY WAIVER: TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE
  LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL THE MAINTAINERS, CONTRIBUTORS, AI AGENTS, OR
  ASSOCIATED ENTITIES BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, SYSTEM CRASHES,
  HARDWARE FAILURE, DATA LOSS, MEMORY CORRUPTION, FINANCIAL LOSS, OR OTHER
  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
  FROM, OUT OF, OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
  DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
- 4.3 NO SUPPORT OBLIGATION: Neither You nor the Maintainers are obligated
  to provide ongoing technical support, maintenance, or bug fixes for any
  Contribution. If it crashes, breaks, or melts a GPU, the sole recourse is
  to inspect the source code and issue a patch.

5. Representations & Mutual Trust

- You represent that you are legally authorized to grant the above licenses.
- You confirm that your Contribution does not knowingly violate any
  third-party intellectual property or trade secret laws.

